  "prefLabel": "Lab 501.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-01-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 501.01 Purpose. This chapter sets forth the policies of the department of labor about how parties in the workers’ compensation process substantially comply with the duty to compute and pay compensation, the method of record keeping and filing of forms, the content and format of forms, the content and handling of medical information, and the procedures for assuring all parties’ rights throughout the workers’ compensation process including hearings and appeals.\n\nSource. #2264, eff 1-6-83; ss by #2935, eff 12-27-84, EXPIRED: 12-27-90\n\nNew. #5235, eff 9-27-91, EXPIRED: 9-27-97\n\nNew. #6631, INTERIM, eff 11-16-97, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6806, eff 7-18-98; ss by #8682, INTERIM, eff 7-15-06, EXPIRED: 1-11-07\n\nNew. #9019, eff 11-1-07; ss by #11067, eff 4-1-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab500.html"
